From 455698a7fa77be86ba7db6b642006783306f25fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:09:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] sparc64: stop cookie IRQ setup after allocation failure

sun4v_build_common() returns zero when the IRQ descriptor or handler
data cannot be allocated. Passing that result to cookie_assign()
dereferences missing handler data for IRQ zero.

Return before assigning the cookie when allocation fails. Keep the
existing irq_free() cleanup for hypervisor cookie-assignment failure.

Fixes: ee6a9333fa58 ("sparc64: sparse irq")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c b/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c
index 3f55c69d5f3b..4f480a8cb66a 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c
@@ -704,6 +704,8 @@ static unsigned int cookie_build_irq(u32 devhandle, unsigned int devino,
 	unsigned int irq;
 
 	irq = sun4v_build_common(devhandle, devino, cookie_handler_data, chip);
+	if (!irq)
+		return 0;
 
 	hv_error = cookie_assign(irq, devhandle, devino);
 	if (hv_error) {
